  "verdict": {
    "headline_lockable": true,
    "why": "Ru spans 0.8128-0.8363 over 5 seeds; even the worst seed exceeds the Krasnov published 0.81. Ir spans 0.8295-0.8597, all far above 0.73. 'Match-or-exceed Krasnov within-metal' is seed-robust, not a lucky-seed artifact.",
    "unresolvable_confirmed_quantitatively": "Os swings 0.3133-0.5867 (spread 0.2733) across seeds -- far larger than Ru/Ir. That swing IS the unresolvability: at n=36 unique ligands the estimate moves more than any method would move it.",
    "tie_rule_caveat": "Every number above is under the default tie rule (ties -> ACTIVE, ``sum*2>=n``). Under the conservative rule Ru spans 0.7880-0.8082 and no longer clears Krasnov 0.81 on every seed -- see metal_activity_transfer_tie_sensitivity.json. So 'Ru beats Krasnov' is seed-robust but NOT tie-rule robust: state it as parity. Ir is robust under either rule."
  },
  "supersedes": {
    "path": "metrics/by_metric/metal_activity_transfer_seed_stability.json",
    "reason": "The superseded artifact's cross_metal_per_seed covers only 3 of its 5 seeds (the sweep was still running when it was written) and its producer was an ad-hoc workflow script that no longer exists. Preserved verbatim per AGENTS.md \u00a75.5."
  }
